-- Passage rg11-story-details-inference-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a952bb97-3d84-5d6b-b622-89a2478549ae', 'rg11-story-details-inference-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-story-details-inference'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Anchor Leg$q$, $q$My sister runs the third leg, and I run last.
For two seasons she has handed me the baton
the way a person hands over a full glass of water,
careful, a little late, never looking at my face.

Coach says the exchange zone is twenty meters long.
Coach says trust is a distance you can measure.
I have measured it in scuffed chalk and in the space
between her breathing and my name.

Tonight the stands are half empty and cold.
Nobody here will remember the time on the board.
She comes around the curve with her chin too high,
the way she runs when her legs have already quit
and only the rest of her is still deciding.

I start late. I am not supposed to start late.
I reach back with my hand open and my eyes ahead,
and for one long stride there is nothing in it,
only the night air and the sound of her shoes.

Then the baton is there, warm from her grip,
and I hear her say one word I will not repeat,
because it was for me and it was not about the race.

I do not win. I do not need to look
to know she has stopped at the edge of the lane,
hands on her knees, watching me all the way in.$q$, 'draft')
