   $q$Which evidence best supports the inference that Felix deeply respects Dr. Kowalczyk?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He checks the fat under the warbler's feathers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"He took over the station after she retired from it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"He copies her habit of writing data on his hand and mentions her often.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He types the band number into the laptop with one finger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He copies her habit of writing data on his hand and mentions her often.$q$, $q$Keeping a habit "picked up from the woman who trained him" and mentioning her "about once an hour" show lasting admiration. Taking over the station is a fact about his job and says nothing on its own about his feelings.$q$, 'draft', 'fd3f5dd4-461b-5acd-94af-e352d8c76197')
