   $q$Which question does the poem raise but leave unanswered?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Who wrote the earlier pencil lines on the doorframe.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Whether the speaker took a photograph of the marks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"When the landlord planned to paint the apartment.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Why the family stopped recording heights on the frame.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Why the family stopped recording heights on the frame.$q$, $q$The speaker hopes a future tenant will "wonder ... why they stopped measuring," and the poem never explains the reason. The earlier lines are in "my father's careful print," so their writer is stated.$q$, 'draft', '2cf481d5-3cf4-5436-a134-7e4cbc0c6080')
