values
  ('a19925da-b954-5594-a7cd-31064221f7de', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-story-details-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The narrator says travelers left pleased, "having bought something they could not carry." What does this phrase suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They were tricked into paying for a heavy object they never received.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-inference"},{"text":"They bought too many goods to carry and left some behind in the canyon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They felt angry about the price once they had left the canyon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They paid for an experience, and the phrase hints at the oddness of the deal.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They paid for an experience, and the phrase hints at the oddness of the deal.$q$, $q$An echo is a sound, not an object, so the phrase gently points out that travelers paid for something intangible. They went away "pleased," which rules out the reading that they felt cheated or angry.$q$, 'draft', '6ca79473-7f0b-539b-8f69-1fa6e082c138')
