   $q$What can be inferred from the fact that Mei-Lin looked at the clock "for what felt like a long while" before raising her hand?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She was waiting for Dario to notice the mistake first.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She was unsure how to read the numbers on the clock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She hoped the arbiter would walk by on his own.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She knew reporting it would cost her an edge she needed.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She knew reporting it would cost her an edge she needed.$q$, $q$She needs a win to qualify, and the narrator notes that fifteen minutes "is a great deal of time in a close game," so her pause shows she weighed that advantage. She read the clock correctly at a glance, so confusion is not the reason.$q$, 'draft', '79af5ab3-d9e4-57f8-b7c8-5744625a1d25')
