   $q$Why does Mei-Lin most likely tell her coach about the clock before he can speak?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She wants him to know her choice before he judges the loss.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She wants him to file a complaint about Dario.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She is trying to change the official result.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She blames the arbiter for causing her loss.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She wants him to know her choice before he judges the loss.$q$, $q$She speaks just as he "opened his mouth," so she makes sure he hears what she chose to do before he comments on the result. She does not ask for any change or complaint, and she accepted the loss by tipping her king.$q$, 'draft', '79af5ab3-d9e4-57f8-b7c8-5744625a1d25')
